#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:3
msgid "Cookies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:5
msgid ""
"An **HTTP cookie** (web cookie, browser cookie) is a small piece of data "
"that a server sends to the user's web browser. The browser may store it "
"and send it back with later requests to the same server. Typically, it's "
"used to tell if two requests came from the same browser - keeping a user "
"logged-in, for example. It remembers stateful information for the "
"stateless HTTP protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:11
msgid "Cookies are mainly used for three purposes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:13
msgid ""
"**Session management**: Logins, shopping carts, game scores, or anything "
"else the server should remember"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:14
msgid "**Personalization**: User preferences, themes, and other settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:15
msgid "**Tracking**: Recording and analyzing user behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:17
msgid ""
"To help you efficiently send cookies to browsers, CodeIgniter provides "
"the ``CodeIgniter\\Cookie\\Cookie`` class to abstract the cookie "
"interaction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:27
msgid "Creating Cookies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:29
msgid "There are currently four ways to create a new ``Cookie`` value object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:33
msgid ""
"When constructing the ``Cookie`` object, only the ``name`` attribute is "
"required. All other else are optional. If the optional attributes are not"
" modified, their values will be filled up by the default values saved in "
"the ``Cookie`` class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:38
msgid "Overriding Defaults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:40
msgid ""
"To override the defaults currently stored in the class, you can pass a "
"``Config\\Cookie`` instance or an array of defaults to the static "
"``Cookie::setDefaults()`` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:45
msgid ""
"Passing the ``Config\\Cookie`` instance or an array to "
"``Cookie::setDefaults()`` will effectively overwrite your defaults and "
"will persist until new defaults are passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:49
msgid "Changing Defaults for a Limited Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:51
msgid ""
"If you do not want this behavior but only want to change defaults for a "
"limited time, you can take advantage of ``Cookie::setDefaults()`` return "
"which returns the old defaults array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:59
msgid "Accessing Cookie's Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:61
msgid ""
"Once instantiated, you can easily access a ``Cookie``'s attribute by "
"using one of its getter methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:67
msgid "Immutable Cookies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:69
msgid ""
"A new ``Cookie`` instance is an immutable value object representation of "
"an HTTP cookie. Being immutable, modifying any of the instance's "
"attributes will not affect the original instance. The modification "
"**always** returns a new instance. You need to retain this new instance "
"in order to use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:77
msgid "Validating a Cookie's Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:79
msgid ""
"An HTTP cookie is regulated by several specifications that need to be "
"followed in order to be accepted by browsers. Thus, when creating or "
"modifying certain attributes of the ``Cookie``, these are validated in "
"order to check if these follow the specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:83
msgid "A ``CookieException`` is thrown if violations were reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:86
msgid "Validating the Name Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:88
msgid "A cookie name can be any US-ASCII character, except for the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:90
msgid "control characters;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:91
msgid "spaces or tabs;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:92
#, python-brace-format
msgid "separator characters, such as ``( ) < > @ , ; : \\ \" / [ ] ? = { }``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:94
msgid ""
"If setting the ``$raw`` parameter to ``true`` this validation will be "
"strictly made. This is because PHP's `setcookie() "
"<https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.setcookie.php>`_ and "
"`setrawcookie() "
"<https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.setrawcookie.php>`_ will reject "
"cookies with invalid names. Additionally, cookie names cannot be an empty"
" string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:101
msgid "Validating the Prefix Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:103
msgid ""
"When using the ``__Secure-`` prefix, cookies must be set with the "
"``$secure`` flag set to ``true``. If using the ``__Host-`` prefix, "
"cookies must exhibit the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:106
msgid "``$secure`` flag set to ``true``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:107
msgid "``$domain`` is empty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:108
msgid "``$path`` must be ``/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:111
msgid "Validating the SameSite Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:113
msgid "The SameSite attribute accepts three values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:115
msgid ""
"**Lax**: Cookies are not sent on normal cross-site subrequests (for "
"example to load images or frames into a third party site), but are sent "
"when a user is navigating to the origin site (*i.e.* when following a "
"link)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:116
msgid ""
"**Strict**: Cookies will only be sent in a first-party context and not be"
" sent along with requests initiated by third party websites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:117
msgid ""
"**None**: Cookies will be sent in all contexts, *i.e.* in responses to "
"both first-party and cross-origin requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:119
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter, however, allows you to set the SameSite attribute to an "
"empty string. When an empty string is provided, the default SameSite "
"setting saved in the ``Cookie`` class is used. You can change the default"
" SameSite by using the ``Cookie::setDefaults()`` as discussed above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:123
msgid ""
"Recent cookie specifications have changed such that modern browsers are "
"being required to give a default SameSite if nothing was provided. This "
"default is ``Lax``. If you have set the SameSite to be an empty string "
"and your default SameSite is also an empty string, your cookie will be "
"given the ``Lax`` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:127
msgid ""
"If the SameSite is set to ``None`` you need to make sure that ``Secure`` "
"is also set to ``true``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/libraries/cookies.rst:129
msgid ""
"When writing the SameSite attribute, the ``Cookie`` class accepts any of "
"the values case-insensitively. You can also take advantage of the class's"
" constants to make it not a hassle."
msgstr ""

